INT. CIRCUS FORTUNE-TELLER'S TENT - NIGHT

Velvet drapes, a round table, a glass ball glowing faintly from within. Incense curls toward a patched canvas ceiling. Outside, a calliope plays something slow and off-key.

MADAME ZORINA PETROVSKAYA-LUND (60s, turban, rings on every finger) lays out tarot cards. Across from her, DETECTIVE MALCOLM OKORO-BRIGGS (40s, damp trench coat, hat in hands) watches. In the corner, a boy, CASPIAN "CASS" WELLES (12, striped shirt, wide eyes) sits on a trunk, holding a cage of white mice.

MALCOLM
Madame, you told the police you saw nothing.

ZORINA
I told the police what they wished to hear.

MALCOLM
And what did you see?

She turns a card. The Tower. Lightning, falling figures.

ZORINA
A man in a gray suit, running from the big top at nine.

CASS
(from the corner)
He had a red scarf.

MALCOLM
Cass, were you there?

CASS
I was feeding the mice.

A TELEPHONE rings, shrill, on a shelf behind the curtain. Everyone stiffens. Zorina rises, parts the drape, lifts the receiver.

ZORINA
(into phone)
Yes.

Malcolm crosses and takes it from her.

MALCOLM
(into phone)
Okoro-Briggs.

SERGEANT (V.O.)
(over the line)
Sir, we found the scarf. Red wool. It was tied to the Ferris wheel.

MALCOLM
Anyone with it?

SERGEANT (V.O.)
No, sir. But the wheel is turning.

Malcolm lowers the receiver. Outside, the calliope stops. In the silence, a distant, iron creak. Zorina's rings click against the glass ball.

ZORINA ^
Detective, do not go out there.

MALCOLM ^
Madame, I have to.
